# Dual platform (web + app) — mandatory sync

When the user builds or changes anything on **one platform**, update the **other in the same change** unless they explicitly say web-only or app-only.

## Roles in scope

- `WORKSHOP_PICKUP_BOY` (pickup & delivery)
- `WORKSHOP_SUPERVISOR` / workshop advisor
- `WORKSHOP_MECHANIC`
- `WORKSHOP_ADMIN` / owner
- `TELECALLER`, `LEAD_MANAGER`, Advanced CRM
- Any other dashboard / role feature the user touches

## Bidirectional rule

| User works on… | You must also update… |
|----------------|------------------------|
| `apps/mobile` (screens, flows, UI) | Matching `apps/web` pages under `/dashboard/...` |
| `apps/web` (pages, components) | Matching `apps/mobile` screens under `src/screens/...` |

Do not wait for the user to ask “web pe bhi karo” or “app pe bhi karo”.

## What to keep in sync

1. **APIs** — Prefer shared routes under `apps/web/src/app/api/...` used by both clients. New endpoints → wire mobile (`ENV.API_URL`) and web.
2. **Business logic** — Mirror helpers in both:
   - Web: `apps/web/src/lib/workshop/pickupTaskFlow.ts`, `pickupPhotos.ts`, etc.
   - Mobile: `apps/mobile/src/lib/pickupTaskFlow.ts` (same function names & behavior).
3. **Flows** — Same steps, gates, dummy-lead bypass rules, notifications, and status handling on both sides.
4. **Dashboard UX** — Same sections (e.g. Fresh leads / Recently completed), filters, counts, empty states, View all targets.
5. **UI parity** — Web must be **mobile-responsive** (phone + tablet). App uses native patterns but same data and actions.

## Pickup boy reference paths

| Concern | Web | Mobile |
|---------|-----|--------|
| Dashboard | `apps/web/src/app/dashboard/workshop_pickup_boy/page.tsx` | `apps/mobile/src/screens/dashboard/WorkshopPickupBoyDashboard.tsx` |
| Tasks | `.../workshop_pickup_boy/tasks/page.tsx` | `apps/mobile/src/screens/pickup/PickupTasksScreen.tsx` |
| History | `.../workshop_pickup_boy/history/page.tsx` | `apps/mobile/src/screens/pickup/TaskHistoryScreen.tsx` |
| Job detail | `.../workshop_pickup_boy/tasks/[id]/page.tsx` | `.../workshop_pickup_boy/PickupJobDetailScreen.tsx` |
| Lead card | `apps/web/src/components/workshop/PickupLeadCard.tsx` | `apps/mobile/src/components/workshop/PickupLeadCard.tsx` |
| Pickup APIs | `apps/web/src/app/api/pickup/**` | Same routes via `ENV.API_URL` |

## Implementation checklist (every feature)

- [ ] API route(s) shared or duplicated with same contract
- [ ] Web page/screen updated
- [ ] Mobile page/screen updated
- [ ] Shared flow helpers updated on **both** sides if status/filter logic changed
- [ ] Notifications / realtime refresh on both if applicable
- [ ] Dummy-test bypass (`L-DUM*` / `DUMMY_SEED`) consistent if pickup-related
- [ ] Web layout tested at mobile breakpoints

## Exceptions

- Pure copy, icons, or platform-specific native permissions (camera, push) — document in the response; still sync the **behavior**.
- User explicitly says **web-only** or **app-only**.
